<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bento Gonçalves</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1788">1788</a>–<a href="/years/1847">1847</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Bento Gonçalves da Silva</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bento Gonçalves was a rancher and soldier of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-grande-do-sul">Rio Grande do Sul</a> who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ragamuffin-war">Ragamuffin War</a>, or Farroupilha, against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Empire of Brazil</a> from 1835. He was elected president of the breakaway Riograndense Republic, though he spent part of the war as a prisoner. The rebels made peace with the empire in 1845, and he is remembered as a hero in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bento-goncalves.jpg" alt="Bento Gonçalves" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Retrato_de_Bento_Gon%C3%A7alves_da_Silva_(Museu_de_Hist%C3%B3ria_J%C3%BAlio_de_Castilhos).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
